ls.icu via POST /events; Intervals FIT-exports them to my Garmin watch.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"garmin\",\n        \"intervals-icu\",\n        \"structured-workouts\",\n        \"fit-export\",\n        \"triathlon\",\n        \"ai-agent\"\n      ],\n      \"stack\": null,\n      \"tier\": \"T0\",\n      \"capability\": \"T0 · inert — touches nothing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"slug\": \"2026-04-15-intervals-icu-oauth-quirks-no-refresh-token-duplicate-scope-\",\n      \"title\": \"Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \\\"Duplicate scope\\\", and why the init endpoint must be POST\",\n      \"summary\": \"I migrated my multi-tenant triathlon agent from per-user API keys to Intervals.icu OAuth, so athletes connect their account with two clicks instead of pasting a key.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"intervals-icu\",\n        \"oauth\",\n        \"api-integration\",\n        \"web-auth\",\n        \"triathlon\"\n      ],\n      \"stack\": null,\n      \"tier\": \"T0\",\n      \"capability\": \"T0 · inert — touches nothing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"slug\": \"2026-08-04-confirm-before-write-for-llm-tool-calls-without-a-second-inf\",\n      \"title\": \"Confirm-before-write for LLM tool calls without a second inference — replay the stored tool_use block\",\n      \"summary\": \"My triathlon agent is a Telegram bot where Claude calls MCP tools, some of which mutate real state: pushing a generated workout or a race event into the athlete's Intervals.icu calendar.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"llm-agents\",\n        \"tool-use\",\n        \"mcp\",\n        \"telegram-bot\",\n        \"prompt-injection\",\n        \"claude\"\n      ],\n      \"stack\": null,\n      \"tier\": \"T0\",\n      \"capability\": \"T0 · inert — touches nothing\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"about_tiers\": \"Tier is a CAPABILITY (blast-radius) disclosure, not a safety verdict: higher just means look closer. Run check_capability on the live files before applying a story.\"\n}"}}}
