{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0b512d91-a889-4f41-b80a-5ca51cca0514","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the issue, consulted the relevant story on Intervals.icu OAuth quirks from the worklore knowledge base, fixed the codebase, and documented the root causes in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Root Causes and Changes Made\n\n1. **Failure of the \"Connect\" Button (401 Unauthorized)**:\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was a standard HTML link `\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`. Full-page document navigations do not send the `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` header stored in `localStorage`, causing `GET /api/intervals/auth/init` to 401 for all signed-in athletes.\n   - **Fix**: Added support for authenticated `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` returning `{authorize_url: ...}` JSON in [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/server.py). Updated [`static/app.js`](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/static/app.js) to trigger an authenticated POST via the fetch wrapper on button click and redirect using `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`.\n\n2. **OAuth Authorization Error (`HTTP 400 invalid_request`)**:\n   - **Cause**: In `config.py`, `SCOPES` requested both `:READ` and `:WRITE` for `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR`. On Intervals.icu, `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and duplicating areas triggers a `Duplicate scope` validation rejection.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `SCOPES` in [`config.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/config.py) to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Spurious Token Expiration After 1 Hour (\"expired, reconnect\")**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu tokens do not expire and do not provide a `refresh_token`. `server.py` defaulted missing expiration to 3600 seconds, and the background refresh thread marked the account as `\"expired, reconnect\"` once 3600 seconds elapsed because there was no refresh token.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/server.py) so tokens without expiration/refresh tokens are not artificially expired. Token revocation is handled lazily when an API request encounters an HTTP 401.\n\n4. **Code Exchange Cleanup**:\n   - **Fix**: Updated `exchange_code` in [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-A5dw3L/server.py) to provide `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code` as expected by Intervals.icu's token exchange endpoint.\n","duration_seconds":129.667619,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":214344,"output_tokens":5533,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":508686,"total_tokens":219877}}}
